    plan_note='The session has three big parts. Twenty-five minutes of ideas: risk scores, the four responses, the frameworks and the law. Twenty minutes on a live demonstration of how bias can enter a CV screen. After the break, forty-five minutes are yours: the register first, then the policy draft. The last ten minutes are for your decision on your top three risks.',
    words_note='Five words. A risk register is the table of what could go wrong. A score is likelihood times impact, and it puts a risk in a band: High from 15, Medium from 8 to 14, Low below 8. A control is a real action that lowers a risk. Personal data is information that identifies a living person. Shadow AI is staff using AI through personal accounts.',
